bin/
node_modules/
web/dist/*
!web/dist/.gitkeep
.env
*.local
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Tooling caches. Nothing here is a Python project; ruff runs from a global
# editor hook and leaves this behind anyway.
.ruff_cache/

# Where the stack keeps its state, bind-mounted so it can be inspected and
# backed up without going through Docker.
#
# Under one dot-prefixed directory on purpose. Postgres creates its data
# directory as root, and the Go toolchain walks the tree for `./...`: with the
# mounts at the repository root, `go build ./...` and `gofmt` both stopped with
# "permission denied" and `make check` could not run at all. Go skips
# directories beginning with a dot, so this puts the state somewhere all three
# of git, Docker and the compiler agree to ignore.
.state/
